VAL_ 767 STATE 0 "NO_FAULT" 1 "FAULT_BAD_CHECKSUM" 2 "FAULT_SEND" 3 "FAULT_SCE" 4 "FAULT_STARTUP" 5 "FAULT_TIMEOUT" 6 "FAULT_INVALID" 7 "STATE_AEB_CTRL" ;

CM_ BO_ 291 "RADAR_HEARTBEAT: Continental ARS (bus 1) liveness frame, 7-byte static payload. Confidence: HIGH (always 00 00 00 00 00 00 2b across 600+ msgs driving + 600+ stationary). Reference: 2026-05-16 RE on route 00000312.";
BO_ 291 RADAR_HEARTBEAT: 7 RADAR
 SG_ STATIC_PAYLOAD : 48|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" XXX

CM_ BO_ 849 "RADAR_STATUS: Continental ARS (bus 1) per-frame status + counter + CRC. Confidence: HIGH structural (B1 counter sig, B6+B7 CRC sig). LOW byte-level for B0/B5 (best-fit only). STATUS_BIT_0..15 are placeholder names for B3+B4 sparse status flags — meanings TBD via fault-injection drives (cover radar, drive multipath, etc.). Reference: 2026-05-16 RE on route 00000312 segs 0-3, Gemini Pro Preview cold handoff. Tesla PR #3011 vocabulary applies once bit→flag mapping is known.";
BO_ 849 RADAR_STATUS: 8 RADAR
